{"archetypes":[{"name":"schema-consumers","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Three JSON schemas are bumped simultaneously (review-summary.json v2→v3, review-and-fix-summary.json v2→v3, tally batches v1→v2) but only files changed in the diff are visible here; callers outside the diff may still hard-code schema_version checks or read neutral_count.","prompt_body":"Examine every file in skills/ and scripts/ that reads from review-summary.json, review-and-fix-summary.json, review-and-fix-summary.json, plan-review-tally.json, or code-review-tally.json and was NOT modified in this diff. Check whether each such reader accesses neutral_count, schema_version == 2, or schema_version == 1 in a way that will silently produce zero or break after the bumps. Also verify that the backward-compatibility guard in review-and-fix.sh that reads .neutral_count via jq -r '.["neutral" + "_count"]' is the only remaining such reader and is correct. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"scoreboard-awk-semantics","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The scoreboard column header was renamed from Neutral/Exon to Exonerated in both tally-code-votes.sh and tally-plan-review.sh, but the awk accumulator still writes both internal neutral and exonerated score_rows entries into the same counter, making the column label semantically inaccurate.","prompt_body":"In skills/review/scripts/tally-code-votes.sh and skills/design/scripts/tally-plan-review.sh, locate the awk block that renders the Reviewer Competition Scoreboard. The column header now says Exonerated (formerly Neutral/Exon), but verify whether the awk neutral[reviewer]++ accumulator still increments for both neutral and exonerated score_rows entries, and confirm whether the printed column value matches what the header claims it counts. Also check whether test-tally-code-votes.sh asserts the new column header and whether any test verifies that a finding with the split-panel (neutral) pattern increments this column correctly under the new name. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
